WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:10.500
86. Saving animals, one species at a time. In the late 1960s, you could spot one if

2
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:16.680
you crossed your fingers for luck and traveled deep into a swamp. By 1985, they were turning

3
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:22.920
up in swimming pools. The American Alligator is one remarkable success story of the American

4
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.820
Endangered Species Act, but there are many more. The Endangered Species Act was passed

5
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:34.500
to protect animals whose populations were dangerously low. It created a list of animals

6
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:40.980
that needed to be protected. The act helped stop or regulate hunting of these animals.

7
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:47.100
It also protected their environments. It has probably saved more than 100 types of animals

8
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:53.540
so far. The American Alligator is one. The bald eagle, the symbol of the United States,

9
00:00:53.540 --> 00:01:02.300
is another. The numbers of bald eagles dwindled to only 417 nesting pairs in 1963, because

10
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.900
humans were hunting them and taking over places they live. The biggest problem, however, was

11
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:15.940
a pesticide called DDT, which affected bald eagles' eggs. DDT was banned in 1973, and

12
00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:21.460
bald eagle populations grew steadily after that. Not only are bald eagles a symbol of

13
00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.540
America, but they are now also a symbol of environmental stewardship, says Michael Dalton

14
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:33.460
of the Audubon Society. The Endangered Species Act has saved wolves, fish, insects, and types

15
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:40.020
of almost every creature that walks, flies, or slithers across North America. The population

16
00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:45.540
of the Virginia Big Eared Bat grew by nearly 10 times in the 20 years since it was listed

17
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:53.260
as endangered, another great success. Treaties like CITES, Convention on International Trade

18
00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:59.460
and Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora, try to do the same. With proper attention

19
00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:05.060
and enforcement, animals like the pangolin and Formosan black bears can become environmental

20
00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.380
success stories, too.
